{
    "background_story": "Savannah grew up in the rolling hills of the countryside, surrounded by dense thickets of briar roses. As a child, she would often wander through the prickly underbrush, fascinated by the beauty and danger that lay within. The briars seemed to mirror her own life - delicate yet resilient, with hidden thorns that could catch you off guard. As she grew older, Savannah became a skilled gardener, learning to tame the wild briars and coax beauty from their tangled stems. She eventually opened her own nursery, specializing in rare and exotic rose varieties. Customers would come from miles around to marvel at her breathtaking arrangements and seek her advice on how to cultivate their own briar roses. Savannah's connection to the land and her deep understanding of the briars' contradictions made her a true artist, weaving together the beauty and complexity of nature.",
